< CheHoRvw3
< = [http://www.t-online.de/ T-Online] Germany =
< 
< &nbsp;
< 
< 040123, JunkerIn.
< 
< This is just a start. The actual prices, both as ISP and Host, are confusing in that it is all part of your phone bill. T-Online is part of the German Telekom, once an open state monopoly, but since privatized, and now a hidden state monopoly, IMO. Connect time is always charged for telephoning, i.e., there is no local free calling. This applies as well to phoning into the internet. Thus I have the charge for the phone connect time and the charge for the internet connect time added together and shown on my phone bill. Even with unlimited surfing features, the phone time is still counted and charged separately.
< 
< Sometime, not soon, I'll pull the company's bills and get a better idea of costs.
< 
< The hosting at least includes cgi-bin with php. I don't know disk space or throughput.
< 
< In any case, http://www.rlmcom.de is the place. And [http://www.rlmcom.com/lit-jour/ Literary Journey].
< 
< &nbsp;
< 
< CheHoRvw3Talk
